
🚗 ROS-Based Temporally Consistent Monocular 3D Reconstruction Using Multi-Frame 3D Priors with MASt3R Integration

This project implements a real-time, temporally consistent monocular 3D reconstruction pipeline using:

Webcam

MASt3R (Monocular 3D reconstruction model)

Temporal Fusion Node (custom ROS2 fusion algorithm)

ICP-based multi-frame alignment

Geometric multi-frame 3D priors

The system reconstructs stable 3D scenes in urban driving environments using only a single monocular camera, achieving improved temporal consistency through multi-frame fusion.

🔥 Key Features
🧠 MASt3R Node (Inference Node)

Runs MASt3R in ROS2 (ONNX/PyTorch)

Outputs per-frame 3D point clouds

Publishes sensor_msgs/PointCloud2

Optimized for videos (512×256)

🔁 Temporal Fusion Node (Core Contribution)

Implements a novel multi-frame fusion strategy:

Temporal Exponential Moving Average (EMA) fusion

Adaptive α blending based on ICP fitness

Temporal multi-frame buffer (5–10 frames)

ICP-based frame alignment (Open3D)

Outlier rejection (statistical + geometric filtering)

Voxel downsampled global map publishing

Chamfer/Overlap/ΔDepth metrics logging (CSV)

.ply snapshot saving every N frames

This module ensures temporal stability, reduces flicker, avoids depth jumps, and maintains structural consistency.

📦 Project Structure
mast3r_ros/
│
├── mast3r_node/
│   ├── mast3r_node.py          # MASt3R inference code
│   ├── model/                  # (Optional) MASt3R ONNX weights
│
├── temporal_fusion/
│   ├── temporal_fusion_node.py # Multi-frame 3D fusion algorithm
│   ├── metrics/                # Logs (CSV)
│   ├── snapshots/              # Fused pointclouds (.ply)
│
├── launch/
│   ├── mast3r_fusion.launch.py # Runs both nodes
│
├── config/
│   ├── camera.yaml             #camera intrinsics
│
└── README.md

🛠️ Installation
1. Clone the repo
git clone https://github.com/AbhayAbhi14/Ros_based_Temporally_consistent_Multi_Frame_3DPrior_MASt3R
cd Ros_based_Temporally_consistent_Multi_Frame_3DPrior_MASt3R

2. Setup ROS2 Workspace
mkdir -p ~/ros2_ws/src
cp -r <repo-name> ~/ros2_ws/src/
cd ~/ros2_ws
conda activate mast3r_ros
colcon build --packages-select mono_reconstruct
source install/setup.bash
./fix_shebangs.sh

3. Install Dependencies
pip install open3d scipy numpy
sudo apt install ros-humble-cv-bridge ros-humble-image-transport

▶️ Running the System
Launch MASt3R + Temporal Fusion
ros2 launch mono_reconstruct webcam_mono_recon.launch.py

Inputs Required:

camera video stream (Live or ROS bag)

Camera intrinsics from camera.yaml

Published Topics:
Topic	Type	Description
/mast3r/points	PointCloud2	Raw MASt3R reconstruction
/fusion/fused_points	PointCloud2	EMA temporally fused cloud
/fusion/global_map	PointCloud2	Accumulated map
📊 Evaluation Metrics (Logged Automatically)

Metrics are written to:

temporal_fusion/metrics/metrics_log.csv


Logged values include:

✔ Chamfer Distance

✔ Point Overlap Ratio

✔ Depth Difference (Δdepth)

✔ ICP Fitness Score

✔ Fusion Stability Score

These are used for validation, comparison, and thesis graphs.

🎨 Visualizing Point Clouds

Launch RViz2:

rviz2


Add displays:

PointCloud2

Choose topics:

/mast3r/points

/fusion/fused_points

/fusion/global_map

📷 Dataset Compatibility

Tested with:

Webcam (2560×1440, 512×256 downsampled)

Oxford RobotCar (monocular sequences)

YouTube driving datasets (webcam format)

📝 Research Goal

This project is developed as part of a thesis:

“ROS-Based Temporally Consistent Monocular 3D Reconstruction Using Multi-Frame 3D Priors with MASt3R Integration.”

The main contributions include:

Temporal consistency using EMA + adaptive weighting

ICP-driven multi-frame registration

Multi-frame priors improving geometric stability

Full ROS2 pipeline integrating MASt3R

